{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-james-004",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 4,
  "title": "James 4",
  "display_title": "James 4",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "james",
  "book": "James",
  "bookName": "James",
  "bookOrder": 59,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 4,
  "sortOrder": 59004,
  "verseCount": 17,
  "aliases": [
    "Jas",
    "Jam",
    "Jm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:4:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "From whence come wars and fightings among you? come they not hence, even of your lusts that war in your members?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 4:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:4:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:4:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Ye lust, and have not: ye kill, and desire to have, and cannot obtain: ye fight and war, yet ye have not, because ye ask not.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 4:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:4:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:4:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Ye ask, and receive not, because ye ask amiss, that ye may consume it upon your lusts.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 4:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:4:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:4:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Ye adulterers and adulteresses, know ye not that the friendship of the world is enmity with God? whosoever therefore will be a friend of the world is the enemy of God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 4:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:4:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:4:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Do ye think that the scripture saith in vain, The spirit that dwelleth in us lusteth to envy?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 4:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:4:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:4:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "But he giveth more grace. Wherefore he saith, God resisteth the proud, but giveth grace unto the humble.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 4:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:4:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:4:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Submit yourselves therefore to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee from you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 4:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:4:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:4:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Draw nigh to God, and he will draw nigh to you. Cleanse your hands, ye sinners; and purify your hearts, ye double minded.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 4:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:4:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:4:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Be afflicted, and mourn, and weep: let your laughter be turned to mourning, and your joy to heaviness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 4:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:4:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:4:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Humble yourselves in the sight of the Lord, and he shall lift you up.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 4:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:4:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:4:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Speak not evil one of another, brethren. He that speaketh evil of his brother, and judgeth his brother, speaketh evil of the law, and judgeth the law: but if thou judge the law, thou art not a doer of the law, but a judge.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 4:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:4:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:4:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "There is one lawgiver, who is able to save and to destroy: who art thou that judgest another?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 4:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:4:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:4:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Go to now, ye that say, To day or to morrow we will go into such a city, and continue there a year, and buy and sell, and get gain:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 4:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:4:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:4:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Whereas ye know not what shall be on the morrow. For what is your life? It is even a vapour, that appeareth for a little time, and then vanisheth away.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 4:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:4:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:4:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "For that ye ought to say, If the Lord will, we shall live, and do this, or that.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 4:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:4:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:4:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "But now ye rejoice in your boastings: all such rejoicing is evil.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 4:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:4:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:4:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Therefore to him that knoweth to do good, and doeth it not, to him it is sin.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 4:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:4:17"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
